# ========================================================================================
# LAST TARGET PROBE
#
# Shows which last target slot a key moves. Razor keeps the general lasttarget apart from
# lastharmful and lastbeneficial, and the loops read lasttarget, so a key that only moves
# lastharmful, Set Last Target (Harmful), goes unseen by them.
#
# Use
#   Stop the combat loop. Press the key to test on a creature (Q, V, Shift+Z), then run
#   this. The Journal shows the serial in each slot, and a slot that holds a creature
#   within 18 tiles gets an overhead over it. Press another key, run it again, compare.
#   4294967295 in a slot means Razor took the name for a plain word, not an alias
#   (document/scripting/razor.md part 3), so that alias does not exist in this build.
# ========================================================================================

@setvar! var__probe_last lasttarget
@setvar! var__probe_harmful lastharmful
@setvar! var__probe_beneficial lastbeneficial
sysmsg "Probe: lasttarget={{var__probe_last}} lastharmful={{var__probe_harmful}} lastbeneficial={{var__probe_beneficial}}" 88

if find lasttarget ground -1 -1 18 as alias__probe_last
    overhead "[ last, here ]" 1288 alias__probe_last
endif

if find lastharmful ground -1 -1 18 as alias__probe_harmful
    overhead "[ harmful, here ]" 1288 alias__probe_harmful
endif
